# Python Services (Proxy + Detection)

## Stack

- Python 3.11, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, httpx, structlog, SQLAlchemy async, ruff, mypy strict

## Conventions

- Use `from __future__ import annotations` in new modules
- Settings via `pydantic-settings` in `proxy/app/config.py` — never hardcode URLs/secrets
- Logging: `structlog.get_logger()` with structured key=value fields
- Async DB: `AsyncSession` from `proxy/app/database.py` with `get_db` dependency
- Shared models live in `proxy/app/models.py` — detection imports from proxy, not vice versa

## Detection pipeline

- Each detector in `detection/app/detectors/` returns spans with `category`, `confidence`, `start`, `end`
- `risk_scorer.py` aggregates; category multipliers and role modifiers are intentional — don't flatten
- New detectors must be wired in `detection/app/main.py` parallel pipeline
- Target latency: <5ms p95 for detection path (cache-friendly)

## Policy engine

```python
# Policies only escalate — never downgrade detection action
if policy_action.rank > detection_action.rank:
    final_action = policy_action
```

## Testing

- Tests in `tests/` — use pytest-asyncio (`asyncio_mode = auto`)
- E2E policy tests: `tests/test_policy_e2e.py`
- Run: `poetry run pytest` or `scripts/run_feature_tests.sh`

## Lint

- Line length 100, ruff rules E/F/I/N/W/UP/B/SIM
- Fix with `poetry run ruff check --fix`
